---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Demo from '../components/Demo.astro';
import fadeWidth from '../demos/fade-width.html?raw';
import prefixStyle from '../demos/prefix-style.html?raw';

const themes = { light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' } as const;
const variables = [
  ['--sabi-fade-width', '22px', 'How far each fade reaches into the field.'],
  ['--sabi-fade-solid', '8px', 'The part of the fade, at the very edge, that is fully hidden. A caret scrolled this far is hidden too.'],
  ['--sabi-caret-penetration', '4px', 'How far the caret may enter a fade before the text scrolls.'],
  ['--sabi-edge-gutter', '8px', 'Space between the text and the edges when nothing is hidden.'],
];
---

<Docs title="Styling">
  <h2>Variables</h2>
  <p>Set these on <code>sabi-input</code> or any ancestor, in <code>px</code>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th></th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {variables.map(([name, value, description]) => (
        <tr><td><code>{name}</code></td><td><code>{value}</code></td><td>{description}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <Demo code={fadeWidth} />

  <h2>Prefix</h2>
  <p>The prefix is your own element, so it takes any style. Prefixes and suffixes are dimmed by default.</p>
  <Demo code={prefixStyle} />

  <h2>Your rules win</h2>
  <p>Sabi's styles sit in a cascade layer named <code>sabi</code>, so any rule of yours overrides them without a specificity fight.</p>
  <p>To ship the CSS yourself, for example under a strict content security policy, import the element without its styles and load the stylesheet your own way:</p>
  <Code code={`import { define } from 'sabi-input/core';\nimport 'sabi-input/styles.css';\n\ndefine();`} lang="js" themes={themes} defaultColor={false} />

  <h2>iPhone selection handles</h2>
  <p>iOS draws selection handles inside the text strip, so they are cut off at the edge of your field box, following its corners. iOS rounds that edge to whole pixels: if the box is a fractional height, such as <code>16px</code> text at a line height of <code>1.4</code>, a sliver shows between the handle and a focus ring. A line height in whole pixels, like <code>24px</code>, keeps them flush.</p>

  <h2>Fade state</h2>
  <p>While text is hidden on a side, the element has <code>data-fade-left</code> or <code>data-fade-right</code>. The same state is named by reading direction too, as <code>data-fade-start</code> and <code>data-fade-end</code>, which swap sides in right-to-left text. Use them to style anything else that should react, such as the field around it.</p>
</Docs>
